:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1000066">10.1371/journal.pmed.1000066</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19399157</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000072-Msellem1"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Msellem</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000e5;rtensson</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rotllant</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhattarai</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Str&#x000f6;mberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Influence of rapid malaria diagnostic tests on treatment and health outcome in fever patients, Zanzibar&#x02014;A crossover validation study.</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>e1000070</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1000070">10.1371/journal.pmed.1000070</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19399156</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000072-Assefa1"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Assefa</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Jerene</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lulseged</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ooms</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Damme</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Rapid scale-up of antiretroviral treatment in Ethiopia: Successes and system-wide effects.</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>e1000056</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1000056">10.1371/journal.pmed.1000056</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19399154</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000072-Marchal1"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marchal</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Cavalli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kegels</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Global health actors claim to support health system strengthening&#x02014;Is this reality or rhetoric?</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>e1000059</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1000059">10.1371/journal.pmed.1000059</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19399158</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000072-Reidpath1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reidpath</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Morel</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mecaskey</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Allotey</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>The Millennium Development Goals fail poor children: The case for equity-adjusted measures.</article-title><source>PLoS Med</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>e1000062</fpage><comment>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1371/journal.pmed.1000062">10.1371/journal.pmed.1000062</ext-link></comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19399155</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p>The authors' individual competing interests are at <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.plosmedicine.org/static/editorsInterests.action">http://www.plosmedicine.org/static/editorsInterests.action</ext-link>. PLoS is funded partly through manuscript publication charges, but the <italic>PLoS Medicine</italic> Editors are paid a fixed salary (their salary is not linked to the number of papers published in the journal).</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p>The authors are each paid a salary by the Public Library of Science, and they wrote this editorial during their salaried time.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Provenance:</bold> Written by editorial staff; not externally peer reviewed</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>